    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the owner API response, computed as a single Luhn check digit over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Added a public static `luhn(String)` helper implementing the standard Luhn check digit (ignores non-digit characters, doubles the rightmost digit first), matching the algorithm the acceptance test uses. It's placed here alongside the other derived-field helpers so MapStruct doesn't mistake it for an implicit mapping method.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that computes `OwnerLocality.luhn(customerCode)`, returning `null` when the owner has no customer code.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
